### 1. Execute the automated scraper (Will auto-save into DB!)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/gifts/scrape/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amazon_url": "https://amazon.com"
}

### 2. View all wishlists in the system
GET http://localhost:8000/api/wishlists/
Accept: application/json

### 3. Initialize a new Wishlist container (Assuming user_id 1 is your admin)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/wishlists/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": 1,
  "name": "Holiday Shopping Ideas"
}

### 4. Append the scraped product to the Wishlist container (Assuming list ID 1 and present ID 1)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/wishlists/1/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "present_id": 1,
  "action": "add"
}

### 5. View the final contents inside that specific Wishlist
GET http://localhost:8000/api/wishlists/1/
Accept: application/json
### Register a new separate developer user account
POST http://localhost:8000/api/auth/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alex_gift_finder",
  "password": "super_secret_password_123"
}

### Login with that account to fetch your token string
POST http://localhost:8000/api/auth/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alex_gift_finder",
  "password": "super_secret_password_123"
}

### GET Request: Download your wishlist directly as a clean CSV table file
# (Open this link in your browser to verify the instant file download)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/wishlists/1/export/csv/

### GET Request: Stream out a clean, structured JSON format of your wishlist data
GET http://localhost:8000/api/wishlists/1/export/json/
Accept: application/json

### POST Request: Simulate running the price drop automation on a present (Assuming present ID is 1)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/gifts/1/price-check/
Content-Type: application/json

### GET Request: View the first page containing only 2 items
GET http://localhost:8000/api/gifts/?page=1&items_per_page=2
Accept: application/json

### GET Request: View the second page of data chunks
GET http://localhost:8000/api/gifts/?page=2&items_per_page=2
Accept: application/json

